  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Al0.3CoCrFeNi can exist as a single-phase FCC high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5314382::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HfNbTaTiZr is a BCC high-entropy alloy system.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid solidification produces an effectively random solid-solution state in the proposed alloys.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled annealing treatment can induce a calibrated amount of nanoscale chemical short-range order without causing coarse phase separation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The annealing treatment can produce stable, finely dispersed SRO domains or SRO precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical SRO impedes dislocation motion and can function as a dislocation-pinning microstructure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard",
        "PMC9645729::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO particularly impedes edge dislocations in some high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Induced SRO enhances strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO domains or precipitates deflect and blunt propagating cracks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In BCC HfNbTaTiZr, SRO makes the alloy stiffer and harder.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "In BCC HfNbTaTiZr, SRO increases the plastic-zone size and dislocation density and suppresses twinning under simulated nanoindentation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "In model CrCoNi, SRO increases maximum strength, reduces faulting and structural transformation, and intensifies planar slip and strain localization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9645729::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "In FCC Al0.3CoCrFeNi, strong strain hardening is associated with resistance to shear localization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5314382::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO engineering will increase yield strength by approximately 10–20% relative to the random untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard",
        "PMC9645729::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO engineering will increase Young's modulus by approximately 10–20% relative to the random untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO engineering will improve ductility relative to the random untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO engineering will improve fracture toughness relative to the random untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled SRO will simultaneously improve strength, ductility, Young's modulus, and fracture resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11032334::webcard",
        "PMC9645729::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under typical processing conditions, SRO in NiCoCr may be negligible or have no systematic measurable effect on strength.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7237450::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over-aging, precipitate coarsening, or undesirable phase transformations can eliminate the proposed mechanical-property benefits.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
